<article class="env-lemma" id="0BAN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BAN">Lemma <span data-tag="0BAN">66.10.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. The following quantities are equal: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The dimension of $X$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The supremum of the dimensions of the local rings of $X$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The supremum of $\dim _ x(X)$ for $x \in |X|$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The numbers in (1) and (3) are equal by Definition <a href="/tag/04N6" data-tag="04N6">66.9.2</a>. Let $U \to X$ be a surjective étale morphism from a scheme $U$. The supremum of $\dim _ x(X)$ for $x \in |X|$ is the same as the supremum of $\dim _ u(U)$ for points $u$ of $U$ by definition. This is the same as the supremum of $\dim (\mathcal{O}_{U, u})$ by Properties, Lemma <a href="/tag/04MU" data-tag="04MU">28.10.2</a>. This in turn is the same as (2) by definition. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>